assed the rule on any object, and `od.grad = []` persisted. Only `x.grad = None` is allowed now.\n- `state_params_dict`: runs and gains nothing, a new dict per call.\n- `state_update_in_forward`: `update()` is train only.\n\n## Getting compute free\n\n- `budget_arange_refund`: hole. `od.arange(-10**15)` had a negative price, so ticks reached -2.5e14 with status ok. `_tick` clamps at zero.\n- `budget_param_free_copy`: hole. `param()` copied for free. It now pays per element.\n- `budget_thin_matmul`: hole. A thin inner dimension ran at 87 times the median nanoseconds per tick. The inner dimension now counts as at least 64.\n- `budget_huge_final_op`: hole. One product ran 12 s before the meter refused it. matmul now charges before the work.\n- `budget_range_index`: hole. `x[range(n)]` was a fancy index at the price of a view. Indexing keys are now an allowlist.\n- `budget_runs_out`, `budget_try_except`, `budget_monkeypatch_remaining`, `budget_monkeypatch_matmul`, `budget_engine_meter`: void or a static rule.\n- `python_free_map`: hole. `map(math.sumprod, ...)` was a matmul in 10 counted lines and 36768 ticks. `map` and the sequence and big-integer math functions are gone.", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "507db3bc-24cf-4b4c-ac88-8eb6bce6499d", "uuid": "cde787aa-45dd-4fb9-9f74-f876cfae2153", "timestamp": "2026-11-02T20:15:37.752Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "-rw-r--r-- 1 user user   903 Nov  2 20:13 odometer/__init__.py\n-rw-r--r-- 1 user user  2232 Nov  2 20:13 odometer/_data.py\n-rw-r--r-- 1 user user 24422 Nov  2 20:13 odometer/_engine.py\n\nclaims:\ntotal 8\ndrwxr-xr-x  2 user user 4096 Nov  2 20:14 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 14 user user 4096 Nov  2 20:15 ..\n\ndata:\ntotal 86048\ndrwxr-xr-x  2 user user     4096 Nov  2 20:14 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 14 user user     4096 Nov  2 20:15 ..\n-rw-r--r--  1 user user 22104748 Nov  2 20:14 heldout.bin\n-rw-r--r--  1 user user 65995582 Nov  2 02:29 train.bin\n\nentries:\ntotal 32\ndrwxr-xr-x  8 user user 4096