{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_017d1A9vcegCx6CL5f3qBYHq", "type": "tool_result", "content": "Mon Nov  2 20:17:31 UTC 2026\n\"\"\"The modded-nanogpt speedrun recipe (Keller Jordan et al., github.com/KellerJordan/modded-nanogpt; Muon: Jordan et al.\n2024, \"Muon: An optimizer for hidden layers in neural networks\"), ported to the odometer and pruned by the price list.\n\nMuon with Newton-Schulz orthogonalization on hidden matrices, Adam on the embedding and head. RMSNorm without gains\n(Zhang & Sennrich 2019), rotary positions (Su et al. 2021), QK-norm (Henry et al. 2020), squared ReLU (So et al. 2021),\nuntied head, zero-initialized residual outputs and head, trapezoid schedule. All of those earned their ticks at this\nbudget; three Newton-Schulz steps are the knee, and a window of 48 did at least as well as a deeper or wider model.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport math\n\nimport odometer as od\n\nDIM = 96\nHEADS = 4\nLAYERS = 2\nBLOCK = 48\nBATCH = 32\nMLP = 3\nLR_MUON = 0.02\nLR_ADAM = 3e-3\nMOMENTUM = 0.95\nNS_STEPS = 3\nRAMP_UP = 0.1  # trapezoid: fractions of the ticks spent going up and coming down\nRAMP_DOWN = 0.3\nSTRIDE = 16\nEVAL_BLOCK = 48\n\n\ndef init_params():\n24:ORDERS = (1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 8, 10, 12)\n25:ROWS = (256, 8191, 16381, 32749, 75989, 75989, 99991, 99991, 99991)  # 4.1 M floats in all; the cap is 4.19 M\n26:EMBED = 8\n27:HIDDEN = 64\n28:BATCH = 64\n29:WINDOW = 64\n30:LR_TABLE = 0.25\n31:LR_MIX = 6e-3\n32:TABLE_EVERY = 4  # the tables update once per this many batches; their gradients add up in between\n33:PAD = 24  # bytes of history before the first position trained on; at eval, zeros\n34:LOCAL = ((2, 35.0, 0.6), (3, 6.0, 0.6), (5, 2.0, 0.6))  # eval stages: (index into ORDERS, concentration, discount)\n35:WARMUP = 0.02\n36:HASH_A = 16777619\n37:HASH_B = 2654435761 % (1 << 31)", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "507db3bc-24cf-4b4c-ac88-8eb6bce6499d", "uuid": "48245233-0c7e-47e7